Q: Checking if a blob exists in Azure Storage A: <p>The new API has the <code>.Exists()</code> function call.  Just make sure that you use the <code>GetBlockBlobReference</code>, which doesn't perform the call to the server.  It makes the function as easy as:</p>
<pre><code>public static bool BlobExistsOnCloud(CloudBlobClient client, 
    string containerName, string key)
{
     return client.GetContainerReference(containerName)
                  .GetBlockBlobReference(key)
                  .Exists();  
}
</code></pre>
